1
00:05:12,352 --> 00:05:18,352
Unmask the truth.

2
00:10:24,705 --> 00:10:30,705
The Batman is a crime, mystery, thriller film directed by Matt Reeves.

3
00:15:37,058 --> 00:15:43,058
In his second year of fighting crime, Batman uncovers corruption in Gotham City that
connects to his own family while facing a serial killer known as the Riddler.

4
00:20:49,411 --> 00:20:55,411
Bruce Wayne / The Batman, played by Robert Pattinson.

5
00:26:01,764 --> 00:26:07,764
Selina Kyle, played by Zoë Kravitz.

6
00:31:14,117 --> 00:31:20,117
Lt. James Gordon, played by Jeffrey Wright.

7
00:36:26,470 --> 00:36:32,470
Oz / The Penguin, played by Colin Farrell.

8
00:41:38,823 --> 00:41:44,823
The Riddler, played by Paul Dano.

9
00:46:51,176 --> 00:46:57,176
Carmine Falcone, played by John Turturro.

10
00:52:03,529 --> 00:52:09,529
The Batman is a 2022 American superhero film based
on the DC Comics character Batman.

11
00:57:15,882 --> 00:57:21,882
Directed by Matt Reeves from a screenplay he wrote with Peter
Craig, it is a reboot of the Batman film franchise.

12
01:02:28,235 --> 01:02:34,235
Robert Pattinson stars as Bruce Wayne / Batman alongside Zoë Kravitz, Paul Dano, Jeffrey
Wright, John Turturro, Peter Sarsgaard, Andy Serkis, and Colin Farrell.

13
01:07:40,588 --> 01:07:46,588
The film sees Batman, in his second year fighting crime in Gotham City, uncover corruption with ties to his own
family while pursuing the Riddler (Dano), a mysterious serial killer targeting the city's elite.

14
01:12:52,941 --> 01:12:58,941
Reeves and Dylan Clark produced the film for DC Films and Warner Bros.

15
01:18:05,294 --> 01:18:11,294
A Batman film for the DC Extended Universe (DCEU) franchise was announced in
October 2014, with Ben Affleck starring as the character.

16
01:23:17,647 --> 01:23:23,647
He signed on to also direct, produce, and co-write The Batman by 2016, but had
reservations about the project and stepped down in January 2017.

17
01:28:30,000 --> 01:28:36,000
Reeves took over the following month and reworked the story, removing the DCEU connections to focus on a
younger version of the character earlier in his vigilante career compared to Affleck's portrayal.

18
01:33:42,352 --> 01:33:48,352
Reeves worked on the script with Craig and Mattson Tomlin, and sought to explore Batman's detective aspects more than previous films, drawing inspiration from
the films of Alfred Hitchcock and the New Hollywood era, and comics such as "Year One" (1987), The Long Halloween (1996–97), and Ego (2000).

19
01:38:54,705 --> 01:39:00,705
Following Affleck's departure as the star in January 2019, Pattinson was
cast in May, and additional actors joined later that year.

20
01:44:07,058 --> 01:44:13,058
Filming took place from January 2020 to March 2021 and was halted
for several months due to the COVID-19 pandemic.

21
01:49:19,411 --> 01:49:25,411
The production occurred throughout the United Kingdom, including on
location in England and Scotland, as well as at Warner Bros.

22
01:54:31,764 --> 01:54:37,764
Studios Leavesden.

23
01:59:44,117 --> 01:59:50,117
Cinematographer Greig Fraser shot the film with Industrial Light & Magic's StageCraft virtual
production technology, while Michael Giacchino composed the musical score.

24
02:04:56,470 --> 02:05:02,470
The film has over 1,500 visual effects shots and is one
of the longest superhero films ever made.

25
02:10:08,823 --> 02:10:14,823
After facing multiple delays caused by the COVID-19 pandemic, The Batman was theatrically released in the
United States on March 4, 2022, three days after premiering at the Lincoln Center in New York City.

26
02:15:21,176 --> 02:15:27,176
The film received positive reviews from critics, with praise for Reeves's approach, the performances of Pattinson and
Kravitz, and the cinematography and score, although the tone, runtime, and third act received some criticism.

27
02:20:33,529 --> 02:20:39,529
It was a commercial success, grossing over $772 million worldwide against a $185–200 million budget, making it
the seventh-highest-grossing film of 2022 and Warner Bros.'s highest-grossing pandemic release.

28
02:25:45,882 --> 02:25:51,882
Its financial performance set several pandemic-era box office
records, particularly for IMAX screenings.

29
02:30:58,235 --> 02:31:04,235
The film was nominated for three Academy Awards and
received numerous other accolades.

30
02:36:10,588 --> 02:36:16,588
The Batman is intended to start a trilogy and the
"Batman Epic Crime Saga" franchise.

31
02:41:22,941 --> 02:41:28,941
A sequel, The Batman: Part II, is scheduled for release on October 1, 2027, while a spin-off
television series starring Farrell, The Penguin, debuted on HBO in late 2024.

32
02:46:35,294 --> 02:46:41,294
The film explores themes of police, psychopath, secret
identity, crime fighter, superhero.

33
02:51:47,647 --> 02:51:53,647
The tone is intense and dark and mind_bending.
